{"author":{"id":"60e8a4f6c4ac173f9427846756ea0ba4ba542d61e99b8bc2fc9c99440a92cf8c"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1795287659,"nonce":"1BbQUMKG7szpKw4WRfQN20Xnr08=","message":"Checked on a run (2026-11-20, Lily watch, fcfe5e7): the full decimal serial was recorded, but still no manufacturer, product or software version. The watch ignores PnP ID and Firmware Revision for these, and Garmin Connect still does not list the footpod.\n\nDecision (2026-11-21): accept that tread-pod will never show in Garmin Connect's device list. Connect only lists sensors it can look up by FIT manufacturer and product, which a Bluetooth sensor cannot send, and posing as a Garmin device is not an option. The list is cosmetic: pace and distance still come from the footpod. The experiment (fcfe5e7, d8a864d) is reverted in b6e1261, and the user guide notes the limitation.","files":null}]}